# zdesk's keys (DESIGN D38 step 5; docs/man/zdesk.txt "KEYS"). A user's ~/.config/zdesk/keys replaces this file.
# KEYS ACTION [ARGUMENTS]: KEYS in the one keys format's names (display/keys.h): <A-x> the left Amiga key with x,
# <RA-x> the right one, <S-x> Shift, <C-x> Ctrl, <M-x> Alt, joined as <S-A-Left>. The older "lamiga+shift+left" is
# still read.
# Amiga+F1..F10 stay the console switches and cannot be used here.
<A-Return>          terminal
<A-q>               close
<A-m>               minimise
<A-z>               zoom
<A-Tab>             next
<A-Space>           menu
<A-Left>            move -8 0
<A-Right>           move 8 0
<A-Up>              move 0 -8
<A-Down>            move 0 8
<S-A-Left>          resize -8 0
<S-A-Right>         resize 8 0
<S-A-Up>            resize 0 -8
<S-A-Down>          resize 0 8
<A-1>               workspace 1
<A-2>               workspace 2
<A-3>               workspace 3
<A-4>               workspace 4
<A-5>               workspace 5
<A-6>               workspace 6
<A-7>               workspace 7
<A-8>               workspace 8
<A-9>               workspace 9
<S-A-1>             sendto 1
<S-A-2>             sendto 2
<S-A-3>             sendto 3
<S-A-4>             sendto 4
<S-A-5>             sendto 5
<S-A-6>             sendto 6
<S-A-7>             sendto 7
<S-A-8>             sendto 8
<S-A-9>             sendto 9
